Add NVIDIA NVENC (h264_nvenc) H264 encoder for KPipeWire 6.8.3

On NVIDIA the VAAPI driver is decode-only, so H264VAAPIEncoder cannot
encode and KPipeWire falls back to CPU libx264. Add H264NvencEncoder, a
SoftwareEncoder subclass that converts frames to yuv420p and hands them
to FFmpeg's h264_nvenc, which uploads and encodes in hardware.

Uses the 6.8.3 encoder API: options are emitted through
buildEncodingOptions(), and the filter graph is built in initialize()
because setColorRange() runs after construction. NVENC-valid presets
(p1..p7, tune hq/ll) replace the libx264 ones, which h264_nvenc rejects.
Tried before the VAAPI path; force with KPIPEWIRE_FORCE_ENCODER=h264_nvenc.

